<ptxt>Display range: Momentary interruption - Normal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Momentary interruption: Momentary interruption (open) occurring</ptxt>
<ptxt>Normal: Normal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Related DTC</ptxt>
<ptxt>U0126/63</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Momentary Interruption (M/C Pressure Sensor)</ptxt>
<ptxt>[MMCS]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Indicates momentary interruption (open) status between master cylinder pressure sensor and skid control computer inside actuator assembly</ptxt>
<ptxt>Display range: Momentary interruption - Normal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Momentary interruption: Momentary interruption (open) occurring</ptxt>
<ptxt>Normal: Normal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Related DTC</ptxt>
<ptxt>C1246/46</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Switch to the "Line Graph" display using display switching.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Inspect the 0 (normal) / 1 (interrupted) status on the line graph.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146320J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0 (Normal)</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If it remains 1 (interrupted), inspect the resistance between the skid control computer (built into actuator assembly) ←→ sensor or between the skid control computer (built into actuator assembly) ←→ engine control computer.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>While watching the line graph display, lightly shake the connectors, CAN junction block and wire harness between the skid control computer (built into actuator assembly) ←→ sensor or between the skid control computer (built into actuator assembly) ←→ engine control computer.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146321J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No change in graph</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Even if the harness signal changes from momentary interruption (open circuit) to normal, the ON display on TaSCAN continues for 1 seconds.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the graph changes, there is a momentary interruption in the connector or wire harness, so repair or replace the wire harness and connector.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step2>
</step1>
<step1>
<ptxt>Active Test Inspection</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Turn the IG OFF and connect the SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON and select "ABS/VSC" → "Active Test".</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select the data monitor items to check during the Active Test and press the execute key.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select the Active Test item to perform, press the execute key, and operate the keys specified on the screen to switch each test ON ←→ OFF.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The motor drive stops automatically after approximately 5 seconds to protect the motor, but do not intermittently drive it for several seconds.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Driving of each solenoid is automatically prohibited after approximately 2 seconds to protect the solenoid, and is permitted again after a certain interval.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not depress the brake with only a pressure reduction valve turned ON by itself.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not drive 2 or more solenoids at the same time, except when operating the hold valve and pressure reduction valve of each wheel.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</step2>
</step1>
